+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="faq-2" hidden>
+          <p>Most cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and some kittens or older cats may sleep even more. Their long naps help them save energy for bursts of play and hunting behavior.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example" data-open="false">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
+          <span>Why do cats knead blankets?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="faq-3" hidden>
+          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood. Cats may knead soft surfaces when they feel safe, content, or ready to settle in for a nap.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example" data-open="false">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
+          <span>Do cats recognize their names?</span>
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="faq-4" hidden>
+          <p>Yes, many cats can learn their names and distinguish them from other sounds. They may not always respond, but they often notice when their name is used consistently.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <script>
+    document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((example) => {
+      const button = example.querySelector(".question");
+      const details = example.querySelector(".details");
+
+      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
+        const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
